## Why This Is Asked
Real-world fintech ML requires low-latency scoring, robust drift handling, and strict auditing. The two-tier approach balances speed and accuracy, while feature stores and drift detectors address production reliability. The privacy angle forces region-aware controls and compliant data flows.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time inference with online/offline learning
- Streaming feature stores and windowing
- Calibration and drift detection
- Auditing and privacy/compliance constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: online score update using SGD
let w = initWeights();
for (event of stream) {
  let x = extractFeatures(event); // windowed features
  let p = sigmoid(dot(w, x));
  updateWeights(w, x, label, p);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency under peak load across regions?
- What drift-detection metrics would you track and how would you trigger retraining?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a practical, beginner-friendly ML pipeline for churn with real-world constraints: leakage prevention, encoding choices, and model comparisons that balance performance and interpretability.

## Key Concepts

- Data leakage prevention via time-based or grouped splits
- Handling class imbalance in binary targets
- Baseline vs tree-based models and interpretability
- Evaluation metrics: AUROC andPR-AUC, plus feature importance tools like SHAP

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo baseline pipeline (illustrative only)
function trainBaseline(data){
  const X = oneHotEncode(data.features);
  const {train, test} = timeSplit(X, data.labels);
  const model = trainLR(train.features, train.labels, {C:1.0});
  const preds = model.predict(test.features);
  return evaluate(test.labels, preds);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this for a much larger dataset?
- What monitoring would you set up to detect data drift over time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests on-device ML design under strict latency, privacy, and fairness constraints; requires end-to-end thinking from data flow to deployment.

## Key Concepts
- Edge ML and latency budgets
- Federated learning with DP
- Model compression (quantization/pruning)
- Fairness-aware ranking
- Rollback and drift monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Latency check scaffold (pseudo)
function measureLatency(model, input){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  model.infer(input);
  const t1 = performance.now();
  return t1 - t0;
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit fairness across departments while maintaining DP guarantees?
- What metrics and rollback triggers would you define for drift detection?
